+# -- The Salt Crown of Vael Adrest ---------------------------------------------
+# At Vael Adrest he stopped the tide-siege and the survivors offered him the
+# city's crown. He took the metal and refused the throne, and has worn it jammed
+# down over a road hat ever since so that nobody can mistake it for a claim. So
+# this is a circlet worn OVER the felt and crushed into it - not a coronet
+# sitting neatly under a brim - and the cloth has to GIVE under it (CROWN_BITE_R)
+# or the whole thing reads as a decal printed on the hat.
+#
+# It is also the cheapest silhouette win left on the model: at 184x184 the head
+# is otherwise a smooth dark blob, and an asymmetric spiked crest breaking upward
+# and backward names "ancient king / hierophant" instantly. The spires follow the
+# hat's deliberate 7.5-degree cock instead of quietly correcting it.
+#
+# EVERY number below is sized against ONE test, judged at 184 BEFORE the hero
+# view: the crest has to survive as two or three individually countable hard
+# shapes. Two earlier passes died on that test in different ways - first the
+# blades were too short and lay flat on the felt; then they were tall and splayed
+# but still so narrow they dissolved into grey fuzz at icon size, which is worse
+# than nothing because it fogs the crisp pointed-hat outline that was already
+# working. Width and count are therefore silhouette numbers, not taste numbers.
