+                          # the circlet does not sit square. Deliberate asymmetry
+                          # reads as history; unequal parts with nothing else
+                          # supporting them read as sloppy modelling, so the lean,
+                          # the flattened arc and the snapped blade all have to
+                          # be present together or none of them land.
+# The felt has to visibly GIVE, LOCALLY. A wide shallow squeeze made the whole
+# cone read as narrower and shorter - it cost the hat volume, the exact opposite
+# of the intent - so the squeeze is deep (~26% of the cone radius) but narrow,
+# and the displaced cloth comes back as a roll that OVERHANGS the metal's outer
+# edge far enough to break the light.
+# WHY THIS NEVER RENDERED. Four panels running reported "no crush at all", and
+# four passes answered by making CROWN_DENT bigger, which could not have worked:
+# the failure was SAMPLING, not amplitude. The crown sweep gets its rings from
+# catmull(HAT_SPINE, n), and at the old n=7 the samples near the circlet were
+# ~26 mm apart in z while CROWN_DENT_FALL was 22 mm - the entire waist was
+# narrower than one sample spacing. The five rings covering the whole feature
+# landed at u = -3.22, -1.81, -0.45, 0.87, 2.18, so the waist reached only 81% of
+# its depth and the roll - which peaks at |u| = 1.5 - had NO sample near its crest
