+        mistake: on the front spires the outward splay already points at -Y, so a
+        +Y offset cancels it and leaves the blade standing bolt upright against
+        the felt - which is exactly the "rises up the concave front of the hook"
+        that got the first pass rejected. Rotating preserves the splay on every
+        spire and tips the whole crest back as one piece.
