+        Two different halves. sin a > 0 is the OUTER face and uses a power below
+        1, which fills the section out into a broad flat facet that turns down
+        sharply at each arris; sin a < 0 is the inner face and uses a power above
+        1, pinching it to a keel. That asymmetry is what gives every blade a real
+        lit plane to show the camera instead of a curved surface that shades away
+        to nothing at this size.
